# The CSVs are written by two machines — your laptop and the Lambda — and any
# disagreement about line endings makes git see every line as changed. That
# turned three new rows into a four-file conflict on PR #1. schema.writer()
# pins the writers to \n; this pins what git stores, so a CRLF file arriving
# from anywhere else is normalised rather than committed as a whole-file diff.
*.csv text eol=lf

# Golden frames for the pixel diff are binary; never touch their bytes.
*.ppm binary
